<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Joondalup and Wanneroo cover a big slice of Perth's northern corridor, and Wanneroo is still growing fast. The ABS put it at 246,147 residents in June 2025, up 7,531 in a year, with Joondalup at 176,595. The structural questions owners here ask tend to be practical ones: is this wall load-bearing, why has a crack opened above the laundry door, and what does the council want before it issues a permit for the new patio?</p><p>Kings Park Structural Co is advertising, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to an independent structural engineering firm, which quotes you and contracts with you directly, and that firm pays us for the introduction. Sometimes the most useful first step is finding out whether you need an engineer at all, so start with the <a href="/structural-engineer-cost-perth/">cost guide</a> or call now on (08) 5550 6237.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Joondalup & Wanneroo</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Joondalup & Wanneroo Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Wall removal and beam design</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">About 68% of WA's detached houses are brick, the only state above half, and in double-brick homes some internal walls usually hold up ceilings and roof. The engineer works out what your wall carries and designs the beam, posts and footings your builder needs for the permit.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Crack and structural inspection reports</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">On sandy ground, a leaking pipe or a soakwell dug too close to the house can wash sand out from under a footing. An engineer's report looks at walls, slab and footings, records the cracking or movement and says what it points to.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Patio, carport and shed certificates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A roofed patio or alfresco cover doesn't fit WA's pergola exemption, so check with the City of Joondalup or City of Wanneroo before you build. The engineer's certificate states the site class, design wind speed and the drawings it covers.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Extension and second-storey engineering</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Adding floor area or height takes the work outside the permit exemption, so the building surveyor will want structural drawings. Footing design depends on the AS 2870 site class of your block.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
